<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  LaunchAgent template for the bossclawd memory daemon (M1a Task 8).

  This is a TEMPLATE, not a ready-to-load plist. `scripts/install-bossclawd.sh`
  substitutes the AT-DELIMITED tokens (below) with the ABSOLUTE paths resolved on
  the target machine at install time (launchd/systemd give no user PATH, so every
  path must be absolute — see main.rs and the air-msg installer note). A committed
  plist with hard-coded dev paths would be wrong on every other machine, so the
  real paths are never checked in.

  WHY A LaunchAGENT (per-user), NOT A LaunchDaemon (root):
    The daemon reads the engine DEK from the user's LOGIN Keychain. A root
    LaunchDaemon runs outside the user's login session and cannot reach that
    keychain without a prompt — so this MUST be a per-user LaunchAgent in
    ~/Library/LaunchAgents, started as the logged-in user. This ties directly to
    the Task 0.5 co-signing gate: the Keychain ACL trusts (code-signing identifier
    + certificate leaf), and only the same-user + correctly-signed binary reads
    the DEK silently.

  RunAtLoad + KeepAlive: start at login and relaunch on crash — this is what makes
  the documented "kill the daemon -> it comes back" smoke pass.

  Paths (kept consistent with crates/bossclawd/src/main.rs and
  apps/desktop/src-tauri/src/engine/daemon.rs — do not drift):
    - @BOSSCLAWD_BIN@       the co-signed daemon binary (Contents/MacOS/bossclawd)
    - @STDOUT_LOG@ / @STDERR_LOG@  under ~/Library/Logs (NEVER /tmp)
  The socket + data dir are left at the daemon's defaults on purpose (fewer knobs):
  both the daemon (main.rs resolve_socket_path) and the app (daemon.rs
  resolve_socket_path) default to <app_data_dir>/bossclawd.sock, so they already
  agree without an env override. This unit sets NO env: with pull-based model
  resolution (rung 2, I1) the daemon resolves its own model (signed record ->
  staged English default <data_dir>/models/potion-base-8M). The install script
  STAGES the bundled English model into that default path instead of pinning
  BOSSCLAWD_MODEL_DIR — an env pin would be highest-priority and would block an
  opt-in multilingual language pack.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
  <key>Label</key>
  <string>@LABEL@</string>

  <key>ProgramArguments</key>
  <array>
    <string>@BOSSCLAWD_BIN@</string>
  </array>

  <key>RunAtLoad</key>
  <true/>

  <key>KeepAlive</key>
  <true/>

  <key>ProcessType</key>
  <string>Background</string>

  <key>StandardOutPath</key>
  <string>@STDOUT_LOG@</string>

  <key>StandardErrorPath</key>
  <string>@STDERR_LOG@</string>
</dict>
</plist>
